Colorspace. Purely informative. It will be saved to the file header, but does not affect how chunks are en-/decoded.lib/std/compression/qoi.c3:10:10typestd::compression::qoi::QOIDescstruct QOIDesc { int width, int height, QOIChannels channels, QOIColorspace colorspace }
Descriptor. Contains information about an image.lib/std/compression/qoi.c3:35:8typestd::compression::qoi::TOO_MANY_PIXELSfault TOO_MANY_PIXELSlib/std/compression/qoi.c3:52:2fnstd::compression::qoi::decodefn char[]? decode(Allocator allocator, char[] data, QOIDesc* desc, QOIChannels channels = AUTO)
Decode a QOI image from memory. If channels is set to QOIChannels.AUTO, the function will automatically determine the channels from the file's header. However, if channels is RGB or RGBA, the output format will be forced into this number of channels. The desc struct will be filled with the width, height, channels and colorspace of the image. The function returns an optional, which can either be a QOIError or a char[] pointing to the decoded pixels on success. The returned pixel data should be free()d after use, or the decoding and use of the data should be wrapped in a @pool() { ... }; block. @param data: The QOI image data to decode @param desc: The descriptor to fill with the image's info @param channels: The channels to be usedlib/std/compression/qoi.c3:291:12fnstd::compression::qoi::encodefn char[]? encode(Allocator allocator, char[] input, QOIDesc* desc)
Encode raw RGB or RGBA pixels into a QOI image in memory. The function returns an optional, which can either be a QOIError or a char[] pointing to the encoded data on success. The returned qoi data should be free()d after use, or the encoding and use of the data should be wrapped in a @pool() { ... }; block. See the write() function for an example. @param input: The raw RGB or RGBA pixels to encode @param desc: The descriptor of the imagelib/std/compression/qoi.c3:136:12fnstd::compression::qoi::readfn char[]? read(Allocator allocator, String filename, QOIDesc* desc, QOIChannels channels = AUTO)
Read and decode a QOI image from the file system. If channels is set to QOIChannels.AUTO, the function will automatically determine the channels from the file's header. However, if channels is RGB or RGBA, the output format will be forced into this number of channels. The desc struct will be filled with the width, height, channels and colorspace of the image. The function returns an optional, which can either be a QOIError or a char[] pointing to the decoded pixels on success. The returned pixel data should be free()d after use, or the decoding and use of the data should be wrapped in a @pool() { ... }; block. @param filename: The file's name to read the image from @param desc: The descriptor to fill with the image's info @param channels: The channels to be usedlib/std/compression/qoi.c3:108:12fnstd::compression::qoi::writefn sz? write(String filename, char[] input, QOIDesc* desc)
Encode raw RGB or RGBA pixels into a QOI image and write it to the file system. The desc struct must be filled with the image width, height, the used channels (QOIChannels.RGB or RGBA) and the colorspace (QOIColorspace.SRGB or LINEAR). The function returns an optional, which can either be a QOIError or the number of bytes written on success. @param filename: The file's name to write the image to @param input: The raw RGB or RGBA pixels to encode @param desc: The descriptor of the imagelib/std/compression/qoi.c3:76:8methodstd::compression::zip::ArchiveStreamAdapter.readfn sz? read(&ArchiveStreamAdapter* self, char[] buffer)lib/std/compression/zip.c3:641:29methodstd::compression::zip::ArchiveStreamAdapter.read_bytefn char? read_byte(&ArchiveStreamAdapter* self)lib/std/compression/zip.c3:661:31typestd::compression::zip::CORRUPTED_DATAfault CORRUPTED_DATAlib/std/compression/zip.c3:22:2typestd::compression::zip::ENCRYPTED_FILEfault ENCRYPTED_FILElib/std/compression/zip.c3:24:2typestd::compression::zip::ENTRY_NOT_FOUNDfault ENTRY_NOT_FOUNDlib/std/compression/zip.c3:23:2typestd::compression::zip::INVALID_ARGUMENTfault INVALID_ARGUMENTlib/std/compression/zip.c3:20:2typestd::compression::zip::INVALID_PATHfault INVALID_PATHlib/std/compression/zip.c3:28:2typestd::compression::zip::IO_ERRORfault IO_ERRORlib/std/compression/zip.c3:21:2typestd::compression::zip::PASSWORD_MISMATCHfault PASSWORD_MISMATCHlib/std/compression/zip.c3:26:2typestd::compression::zip::PASSWORD_NEEDEDfault PASSWORD_NEEDEDlib/std/compression/zip.c3:25:2typestd::compression::zip::UNSUPPORTED_METHODfault UNSUPPORTED_METHODlib/std/compression/zip.c3:27:2typestd::compression::zip::ZipArchivestruct ZipArchive { File* file, Allocator allocator, ZipEntryList entries, String mode, String path, String comment }lib/std/compression/zip.c3:51:8methodstd::compression::zip::ZipArchive.add_directoryfn void? add_directory(&ZipArchive* self, String dirname)
