The backed arena allocator provides an allocator that will allocate from a pre-allocated chunk of memory provided by it's backing allocator. The allocator supports mark / reset operations, so it can be used as a stack (push-pop) allocator. If the initial memory is used up, it will fall back to regular allocations, that will be safely freed on `reset`. While this allocator is similar to the dynamic arena, it supports multiple "save points", which the dynamic arena doesn't.lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.c3:13:8methodstd::core::mem::allocators::BackedArenaAllocator.acquirefn void*? acquire(&BackedArenaAllocator* self, sz size, AllocInitType init_type, sz alignment)lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.c3:150:32methodstd::core::mem::allocators::BackedArenaAllocator.destroyfn void destroy(&BackedArenaAllocator* self)lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.c3:56:30methodstd::core::mem::allocators::BackedArenaAllocator.markfn sz mark(&BackedArenaAllocator* self)lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.c3:63:28methodstd::core::mem::allocators::BackedArenaAllocator.releasefn void release(&BackedArenaAllocator* self, void* old_pointer, bool)lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.c3:65:30methodstd::core::mem::allocators::BackedArenaAllocator.resetfn void reset(&BackedArenaAllocator* self, sz mark)lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.c3:74:30methodstd::core::mem::allocators::BackedArenaAllocator.resizefn void*? resize(&BackedArenaAllocator* self, void* pointer, sz size, sz alignment)lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.c3:128:32varstd::core::mem::allocators::DEFAULT_SIZE_PREFIXDEFAULT_SIZE_PREFIX = 8
