The dynamic arena allocator is an arena allocator that can grow by adding additional arena "pages". It only supports reset, at which point all pages except the first one is released to the backing allocator. If you want multiple save points, use the BackedArenaAllocator instead. The advantage over the BackedArenaAllocator, is that when allocating beyond the first "page", it will retain the characteristics of an arena allocator (allocating a large piece of memory then handing off memory from that memory), whereas the BackedArenaAllocator will have heap allocator characteristics.lib/std/core/allocators/dynamic_arena.c3:18:8methodstd::core::mem::allocators::DynamicArenaAllocator.acquirefn void*? acquire(&DynamicArenaAllocator* self, sz size, AllocInitType init_type, sz alignment)lib/std/core/allocators/dynamic_arena.c3:147:33methodstd::core::mem::allocators::DynamicArenaAllocator.freefn void free(&DynamicArenaAllocator* self)lib/std/core/allocators/dynamic_arena.c3:38:31methodstd::core::mem::allocators::DynamicArenaAllocator.initfn void init(&DynamicArenaAllocator* self, Allocator allocator, sz page_size)lib/std/core/allocators/dynamic_arena.c3:30:31methodstd::core::mem::allocators::DynamicArenaAllocator.releasefn void release(&DynamicArenaAllocator* self, void* ptr, bool)lib/std/core/allocators/dynamic_arena.c3:78:31methodstd::core::mem::allocators::DynamicArenaAllocator.resetfn void reset(&DynamicArenaAllocator* self)lib/std/core/allocators/dynamic_arena.c3:124:31methodstd::core::mem::allocators::DynamicArenaAllocator.resizefn void*? resize(&DynamicArenaAllocator* self, void* old_pointer, sz size, sz alignment)lib/std/core/allocators/dynamic_arena.c3:94:33mmethodstd::core::mem::allocators::ExtraPage.is_alignedmacro bool is_aligned(&ExtraPage* self)lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.c3:41:22mmethodstd::core::mem::allocators::ExtraPage.pagesizemacro sz pagesize(&ExtraPage* self)lib/std/core/allocators/backed_arena_allocator.