A RefCounted struct should be an inline base of a struct. If a `dealloc` is defined, it will be called when refcount reaches 0. If `free` is defined, it will be called after `dealloc` otherwise mem::free will be called. For convenience, a ref count of 0 is still valid, and the struct is only freed when when ref count drops to -1. The macros rc::retain and rc::release must be used on the full pointer, not on the RefCounted substruct. So `Foo* f = ...; RefCounted* rc = f; rc::release(rc);` will not do the right thing.lib/std/core/refcount.c3:99:8macrostd::core::mem::rc::releasemacro void release(refcounted)
