Marks a memory region ([addr, addr+size)) as addressable. This memory must be previously allocated by your program. Accessing addresses in this region is allowed until this region is poisoned again. This function could unpoison a super-region of [addr, addr+size) due to ASan alignment restrictions. NOTE This function is not thread-safe because no two threads can poison or unpoison memory in the same memory region simultaneously. @param addr: Start of memory region. @param size: Size of memory region.lib/std/core/sanitizer/asan.c3:53:12macrostd::core::sanitizer::print_stack_tracemacro void print_stack_trace()lib/std/core/sanitizer/sanitizer.c3:17:12fnstd::core::sanitizer::set_death_callbackfn void set_death_callback(VoidFn callback)lib/std/core/sanitizer/sanitizer.c3:24:9varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_LINKER_INITMutexFlags MUTEX_LINKER_INIT = 1lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:5:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_NOT_STATICMutexFlags MUTEX_NOT_STATIC = 256lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:8:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_READ_LOCKMutexFlags MUTEX_READ_LOCK = 8lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:9:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_READ_REENTRANTMutexFlags MUTEX_READ_REENTRANT = 4lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:7:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_RECURSIVE_LOCKMutexFlags MUTEX_RECURSIVE_LOCK = 64lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:12:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_RECURSIVE_UNLOCKMutexFlags MUTEX_RECURSIVE_UNLOCK = 128lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:13:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_TRY_LOCKMutexFlags MUTEX_TRY_LOCK = 16lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:10:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_TRY_LOCK_FAILEDMutexFlags MUTEX_TRY_LOCK_FAILED = 32lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:11:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_TRY_READ_LOCKMutexFlags MUTEX_TRY_READ_LOCK = 24lib/std/core/sanitizer/tsan.c3:14:18varstd::core::sanitizer::tsan::MUTEX_TRY_READ_LOCK_FAILEDMutexFlags MUTEX_TRY_READ_LOCK_FAILED = 56l