.c3:28:22fnstd::thread::channel::create_one_shotfn OneShotChannel*? create_one_shot{Type}(Allocator allocator)
Initialize a one-shot channel for sending exactly one value between threads. The first successful `push` stores the value, and the first successful `pop` receives it. Closing the channel wakes blocked receivers; if a value was already sent before closing, it remains receivable once. Example: ```c3 OneShotChannel{int}* channel = channel::create_one_shot(mem); defer channel.destroy(); Thread thread; thread.create(fn int(void* arg) { OneShotChannel{int}* channel = arg; channel.push(123)!!; return 0; }, (void*)channel)!!; defer thread.join(); int value = channel.pop()!!; ```lib/std/threads/oneshot_channel.c3:40:21fnstd::thread::channel::create_unboundedfn UnboundedChannel*? create_unbounded{Type}(Allocator allocator, sz start_size = 16)lib/std/threads/unbounded_channel.c3:22:23fnstd::thread::channel::create_unbufferedfn UnbufferedChannel*? create_unbuffered{Type}(Allocator allocator)lib/std/threads/unbuffered_channel.c3:19:24fnstd::thread::cpu::native_cpufn int native_cpu()lib/std/threads/os/cpu.c3:71:8macrostd::thread::currentmacro Thread current()lib/std/threads/thread.c3:130:14macrostd::thread::exitmacro void exit(int result)lib/std/threads/thread.c3:131:12typestd::thread::experimental::threadgroup::ThreadFinalizerFnalias ThreadFinalizerFn{Task, Result} { void* finalizer_context, void* init_context }
